{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact O2 head 033c2238c3b25a31ce57cac8651bf31bb413801b on builder/own-agent-membership-20261102, tree b34fa192, for request 28b5cd84 under promise 8f601a58 and review request 551f5cb3. The two own-agent steps, the cohort and the enrollment client hold. One security gap blocks: any member can now open key invitations without a bound, and no one can clear them early.\n\nScope. Main ec48e2d5 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The five commits change 53 paths, and the commit-message check passes for all five. The head touches packages/mcp/src/service.ts, a card path. Card run 41565388797 and Page run 41565388918 succeeded at 5929ca7c. git diff 5929ca7c 033c2238 lists only session-reference-native.test.ts, the note and the five manifests, and none of those is on either workflow's path list. The Card inputs at the head are therefore byte-for-byte the inputs of the run. The service.ts edit only adds this cohort to #applicationRoom, so held request 5de93fbc stays untriggered.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- add-own-agent keeps every add-member guard. It narrows kind to agent and requires the controller to equal the signer. The add-member effects set role to agent for kind agent (membership.ts:458), so the new member cannot take a wider role.\n- own-agent-person-role requires an active person signer at this Membership. It compares the agent role's list with the signer's role list from the open roster, and it refuses when the roster lacks either list. An admin skips the comparison.\n- invite-own-agent-key checks that the member is an active agent, that its role is agent, that its controller is the signer, and the same subset rule.\n- own-agent-capacity refuses once it counts eight active agents with this controller. An agent or a checker cannot sign either step, because the person guard refuses them and the default table withholds membership.own-agent from them.\n- derive/grant.ts:311 refuses every act except a comment from an agent whose controller is inactive. Removing a person therefore stops the agents they added.\n- enrolKey accepts the two new opening kinds only when the link names Membership 13, and every earlier field, controller, key and inbox check still runs.\n- The cohort maps Register 27 to Directory 26 to Membership 13, Rules 10 and Destination 20. Default creation stays unchanged, and R26, D25, M12 and Dest19 stay free.\n\nEvidence. The five manifests hash to 1e361dc0…, 60274b48…, 91893c92…, 278b3186… and 5c60f726…, as the note states. All 87 files match their sizes and digests, they are read-only, and no unit holds an unlisted file. All 115 private raw references in the run records match their files. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match.\n\nThe gate. The qualification meets docs/testing.md at this head. The first gate failed in three files, and 5929ca7c fixed them before a second full gate. The second gate failed only in session-reference-native.test.ts. The follow-up at 63023896 changes only that file, which no other file imports. It adds one import and selects github.com through sessionRoom's existing host parameter. All 24 cases, their deadlines and their assertions stay, and the compiler and the whole owning file pass. Both gates stay failed, as the note says. The change below touches production declarations, so the next head needs a new gate.\n\nChange required:\n\n1. Bound the key invitations that a member can open. Before Membership 13, only admin held membership.invite, so only an admin or the recovery key could open a key item. invite-own-agent-key now gives that power to every member, maintainer and admin, and three facts make it unbounded:\n\n- The step keeps invite-key's only state guard, an active member (membership.ts:384). It accepts any inviteEnds, and the invited key stays live until that deadline (membership.ts:557). The issuer writes 24 hours, but the chain accepts any time.\n- The key item bounds live items at 10,000 for the whole room (membership.ts:275, handlers.ts:295-299). Invited keys count, and so do enrolled keys.\n- revoke-key refuses an invited key (membership.ts:519). Removing the agent stops enrollment, but the invited keys still count until their deadlines.\n\nSo one member with one agent can open invitations with far deadlines until the room holds 10,000 live keys. After that, every key invitation and every person's join refuses, and an admin cannot clear the keys. Add a Native guard to invite-own-agent-key for both parts. Cap the live keys of the agent, invited and active together. O3's first-connection link needs only one. Also bound inviteEnds to a window after the act's time. Add a control for each part, and run a new gate.\n\nNot required. The approved design (73946d0f) listed these guards and missed the key bound too, so this is my miss as well as the head's. Record the bound in the note's decisions.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The own-agent steps stay Native guards in Membership. HTTP and MCP grant nothing, and an exact opt-in cohort carries the new definition.\n\nSecurity: one blocking finding, item 1. No step widens role authority. The subset rule, the controller rule and the capacity rule each hold, and controls 12 and 13 fail at their intended assertions.\n\nSimplification: no change needed beyond item 1.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1276e62a6d18310ffa6133facbca18e1aebdf138","binding":"assigned","head":"033c2238c3b25a31ce57cac8651bf31bb413801b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b6ccec9f2cf30873952a17ad7808d202278bf822\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:168a7588041689d690aa299a043753f3975a8c93\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8f601a58d977510d5acc35aec7fc8cef69dfbd84\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:168a7588041689d690aa299a043753f3975a8c93